        "en": "Directly, requests spread over every node in the data center of the first contact point that answers and move to other nodes when one fails; through SSH, tunnels and forwards the session works through one node. With ScyllaDB on a direct route the session opens a connection per node shard (the shard-aware port 19042) and falls back to the regular port when that is unreachable. Through tunnels keep the nodes on the computer’s local network or use one node. With a local data center set, the contact point must be in it.",
